Z||000000||MooCow||04-05-2001||05:20 PM||||AAAAAAHHHHHHH my car will not start now.  I went out this morning at it started right up.  I let it warm up for like 3 minutes then left for work.  On the way the tach started jumping everywhere, but the car still ran fine.  So I pulled it over and shifted down to second and it turned off.  I tried to re-start it and it turns over but just wont start.  I called my mom on my cell phone to tell her and decided to try it once again and boom it fires right up.  So I drive it to work.  I get ready to go out to eat at and it only turns over.  I checked the battery connections and they work.  The battery doesn't seem to be dead cause it can turn the car over everytime, but the car just will not start.  So is it my starter???  Or something to do with the flywheel??  I need to fix this fast. <BR>                                  Thanks Ken||||reg||11
Z||000001||Stoic||04-05-2001||05:26 PM||||Doesn't sound like the starter.  It sounds more like a sparking problem.  Check the basics(ie. plugs, wires, coil, distributer etc.) and go from there.  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||04-05-2001||05:33 PM||||Doesn't sound like the starter. Sounds like a not getting spark problem.<P>Try unplugging the Tach Filter by unplugging a white connector near the coil (but not directly on the coil). The filter itself is mounted down between the distributor and head on the V6 and I think between the coil and head on the 4. <P>If that's the problem, it should start running. I believe the tach will not work with it unplugged... but you will know it's the problem then.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||04-05-2001||06:20 PM||||Also check your fuel filter. Just the other day, a friend's car was having a similar problem. It would start up sometimes, and sometimes it didn't. And it didn't stay running very long at all. Turned out it wasn't getting enough fuel. Probably not the same problem you have, but just something to check.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||1
Z||000004||pHoOl||04-05-2001||06:22 PM||||Cow, i had the same problem and broke down near Reed City.  It was my distributor having a ring or two rusted out.  Check that, and check the ignition module.<P><BR>PS, wanna cruise sometime? i'm in allendale for school until the end of april.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||06:37 PM||||Id check coil and ign module||||reg||1
