Z||000024||Taijiguy||04-07-2001||08:43 PM||||Dude, your frustration is apparent...but take a breath, and answer some of the questions that have been asked here so you might best take advantage of the massive amount of experience and knowledge that resides here. You have taken much advice, however at this point, there's no new information about what you have actually done. Tell us exactly what all you have done so far. In particular, I'm interested in knowing if you have checked for primary voltage to the coil, and when you check it, you need to check it not just with the key in the run position, but in the start position as well, with the engine turning over. Did you ever remove the tach filter as was suggested? Tell us what you've done so we can help you better.<BR>Good luck!<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000025||MooCow||04-07-2001||10:08 PM||||K now after a day of day of getting away from my car I am all better now.<BR>So far I have replaced the distributor cap and rotor, ignition modual, pick up coil, and the coil.  Jch82 did a spark test with a paper clip of the distributor cap and got nothing, but I am unsure if he did it right.<BR>I have replaced everything now except for the spark plugs and wired, and the distributor itself.  The distrubutor prongs look all rusted so I am now thinking that may be it.<BR>Now where is the tach filter??  Before my car died the tack did jump a lot.  I will be hopefully looking at the car again come tuesday if not wednesday for sure.<BR>Thanks for all of you dealing with me.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||14
Z||000026||Taijiguy||04-07-2001||11:50 PM||||We still don't know if you checked for voltage on the primary side of the coil, that's kind of an important part. (duh) and again, make sure when you check, that you look for voltage with the key in run, but in start as well. Have you by any chance tried to push start the car? ||||reg||1
